 "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "318 never contacts 480 directly (step_06). A time-ignoring route does exist (318->409->733->243->480, from steps 03, 10, 12, 04/13), but it passes through the graph's dominant hub 733 (674 events, 267 out-neighbours, 2641 triangles; steps 07, 12, 15) and other high-degree relays (241: 87 partners, step_14) \u2014 precisely the volume/popularity/static-connectivity confounds that cannot substitute for temporal evidence. Both endpoints are single-shot, low-degree nodes (25 and 26 events with no repeats, step_02), so each relay edge offers only one timestamp to satisfy the 600-unit gap. Critically, every available tool aggregates over the full horizon and exposes no timestamps, so I could neither restrict analysis to [14821, 53221] nor verify ordering and <=600-unit gaps along any candidate chain. Given a repeat ratio of 0.031 and 15.6k edges over 100k time units (step_01), a valid temporal chain is a priori improbable, but I have no direct temporal evidence either way: the correct verdict is insufficient rather than present or absent."}, "raw_final_response": "## Investigation summary\n\n**What I established (static structure):**\n- No direct edge 318\u2192480 exists in the entire horizon (step_06), so any cascade must be multi-hop.\n- Both endpoints are low-activity, single-shot nodes: 318 has 25 events / 25 distinct partners, 480 has 26/26 (step_02) \u2014 essentially no repeated contacts, so each candidate relay edge fires only once and has exactly one timestamp to satisfy the \u2264600 constraint.\n- A static (time-ignoring) route does exist: 318\u2192409 (step_03), 409\u2192733 (step_10), 733\u2192243 (step_12), 243\u2192480 (step_04, step_13). Most such routes are funneled through the mega-hub 733 (674 events, 267 out-neighbours, 2641 incident triangles \u2014 step_07, step_12, step_15) or through hub 241 (93 events, 87 partners \u2014 step_08, step_14).\n\n**Confounder control:** the mere existence of that route is exactly the confound the task warns about \u2014 it runs through the graph's most active hub, whose enormous degree makes static reachability nearly automatic for any node pair. Similarly, high event volume at 241/259/1162 (step_14) explains connectivity without implying influence transfer.\n\n**The decisive gap:** every tool available to me aggregates over the full horizon [0, 100000] and returns no timestamps. I could not obtain event times, restrict any query to [14821, 53221], or test whether consecutive hops of the 318\u2192409\u2192733\u2192243\u2192480 chain (or any alternative) are ordered and separated by \u2264600 units. With ~15.6k edges spread over 100k time units and a repeat ratio of only 0.031 (step_01), typical inter-event gaps on a fixed path are far larger than 600, so the static path is *a priori* unlikely to be time-respecting \u2014 but that is an inference from marginal statistics, not temporal evidence of this cascade.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_fd7e502f\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [318, 480, 409, 733, 243, 241],\n  \"window\": [14821, 53221],\n  \"confidence\": 0.5,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"318 never contacts 480 directly (step_06). A time-ignoring route does exist (318->409->733->243->480, from steps 03, 10, 12, 04/13), but it passes through the graph's dominant hub 733 (674 events, 267 out-neighbours, 2641 triangles; steps 07, 12, 15) and other high-degree relays (241: 87 partners, step_14) \u2014 precisely the volume/popularity/static-connectivity confounds that cannot substitute for temporal evidence. Both endpoints are single-shot, low-degree nodes (25 and 26 events with no repeats, step_02), so each relay edge offers only one timestamp to satisfy the 600-unit gap. Critically, every available tool aggregates over the full horizon and exposes no timestamps, so I could neither restrict analysis to [14821, 53221] nor verify ordering and <=600-unit gaps along any candidate chain. Given a repeat ratio of 0.031 and 15.6k edges over 100k time units (step_01), a valid temporal chain is a priori improbable, but I have no direct temporal evidence either way: the correct verdict is insufficient rather than present or absent.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 38553, "total_output_tokens": 8338, "total_tokens": 46891, "total_latency_ms": 125586, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}